.policy "ruff-n818-error-suffix-on-exception-name" revision 2
.description "Name custom exception classes with an Error suffix, as PEP 8 recommends, unless the exception does not signal an error."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff N818 (pep8-naming): a class whose name does not end in `Error` though one of its positional bases is the
// name `Exception` or `…Error`. Ruff reads the bases as written: a bare name only (parentheses aside), not resolved,
// not `mod.Error`. Names are NFKC-normalised, as Ruff's parser reads them.
//   class C(Exception): ...          ← N818
//   class A(Ｅxception): ...         ← N818: the base is `Exception`
//   class Ｅrror(Exception): ...     not reported: the name is "Error"
//   class D(BaseException): ...      not reported: the base is neither
#include "python/python-20.rerail"

.violation N818(at: node, x: symbol) code "N818"
    "Rename the exception class `{x}` to end in `Error`, e.g. `{x}Error` or swapping an `Exception` suffix for `Error`, and update references; keep it if it signals control flow, not an error."
    suppress ruff "N818"
N818(nm, x) :- kind(c, "class_definition"), field(c, "name", nm), ruff_class_name(nm, x), !suffix("Error", x),
    error_base(c), !ruff_ignored(nm, x).
.decl error_base(c: node)  // a positional base that is the name `Exception` or `…Error`
error_base(c) :- field(c, "superclasses", al), child(al, b0, _), unparen(b0, b), kind(b, "identifier"), text(b, t),
    y = @nfkc(t), (y = "Exception" ; suffix("Error", y)).
